    <name>
        <value>Lifestyle Medicine Sleep Assessment</value>
    </name>
    <description>
        <original_author>
            <item>
                <key>name</key>
                <value>Ricardo Lourenco dos Santos</value>
            </item>
            <item>
                <key>organisation</key>
                <value>Faculty of Medicine, University of Porto (FMUP)</value>
            </item>
            <item>
                <key>email</key>
                <value>ricardolourencosantos@gmail.com</value>
            </item>
            <item>
                <key>date</key>
                <value>2026-01-29</value>
            </item>
        </original_author>
        <lifecycle_state>in_development</lifecycle_state>
        <details>
            <purpose>To record sleep architecture and quality data from consumer wearable devices for lifestyle medicine assessment and sleep disorder screening.</purpose>
            <keywords>sleep, sleep stages, REM, deep sleep, light sleep, sleep efficiency, wearable, sleep tracker</keywords>
            <use>Use for recording sleep measurements including:
- Total sleep duration and time in bed
- Sleep stages: N1 (light), N2, N3 (deep/SWS), REM, Awake
- Sleep efficiency percentage
- Sleep onset latency
- Wake after sleep onset (WASO)
- Sleep quality scores
- Respiratory events during sleep (basic)
- Device provenance and measurement quality

Primary use cases:
1. Nightly sleep summary recording
2. Sleep architecture analysis
3. Sleep disorder screening indicators
4. Longitudinal sleep pattern tracking
5. Correlation with HRV during sleep

Compatible devices: Apple Watch, Fitbit, Oura Ring, Whoop, Garmin, Samsung Galaxy Watch</use>
            <misuse>Not for:
- Formal polysomnography (PSG) replacement
- Clinical sleep apnea diagnosis (requires medical PSG)
- Narcolepsy or parasomnia diagnosis</misuse>
            <copyright>CC BY-SA 4.0</copyright>
        </details>
        <other_details>
            <item>
                <key>licence</key>
